    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/associate-professor-in-urgent-care-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia": {
      "title": "Associate Professor in Urgent Care",
      "description": "Associate Professor in Urgent Care - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Associate Professor in Urgent Care UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Academic LD $174,423 - $192,092 +17% super School of Health Full-Time Part-Time Add to favourites View favourites School of Heath, Sunshine Coast Campus, Sippy Downs Level D, $174,423 - $192,092 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time or Part-time, ongoing appointment The Opportunity Where Passion Meets Impact - Join the School of Health! Are you eager to make a difference in health education and research? Join our dedicated team of researchers and educators at the School of Health (SOH). We have a strong focus on cultivating healthy minds, bodies, and environments through our teaching, research, and outreach efforts. With a purpose that extends regionally and impacts globally, we are committed to advancing knowledge in the health sector and improving the well-being of our communities. Together, let's create healthier communities now and for the generations to come. As Associate Professor in Urgent Care, you will provide academic leadership across the Graduate Certificate in Urgent Care and emerging microcredential offerings. Reporting to the Discipline Lead, Paramedicine, you will lead curriculum innovation, ensuring programs reflect contemporary clinical practice, regulatory standards, and the future direction of healthcare delivery. This is an opportunity to influence how urgent care is taught, practiced, and researched. You will shape learning experiences that are practical, evidence-driven, and outcomes-focused, while also contributing to a strong research culture and mentoring the next generation of academic talent. For more information, please visit us online: School of Health You will: lead the design, delivery and continuous improvement of postgraduate urgent care programs, ensuring contemporary, practice-ready learning; drive a visible research agenda, securing funding and delivering outcomes that influence urgent care practice and policy; mentor and develop academic staff, strengthening teaching excellence and research capability across the discipline; and build strategic partnerships and contribute to academic governance, enhancing program quality, relevance and impact within the School About you: You are an established academic leader with national standing in your discipline and a passion for shaping the future of urgent care education. You combine scholarly rigour with practical insight, and you thrive in environments where you can influence, mentor, and build. You bring a collaborative mindset, strong industry engagement, and a clear vision for how education and research can improve healthcare delivery and outcomes. You will possess: Demonstrated leadership in learning and teaching, including curriculum innovation and student success outcomes Experience mentoring academic staff and building research and teaching capability Evidence of meaningful contribution to your discipline at a national level Proven ability to develop and maintain strategic partnerships across healthcare, industry, and community sectors Extensive experience in academic governance and university-level administration A commitment to inclusive, culturally safe, and student-centred education Postgraduate qualifications in higher education and formal recognition for excellence in research and/or teaching (desirable) UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. Position description: 494689_Associate Professor Urgent Care.pdf UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 8 November 2026 Your completed application must include: a resume, and a response to selection criteria. Noting that within the application form, we will request a statement addressing each of the selection criteria contained within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Associate Professor Nigel Barr Discipline Lead, Paramedicine Phone: 07 5456 5020 Email: nbarr@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Trials Associate - Pharmacy Health Hub Morayfield Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Join UniSC Clinical Trials at Health Hub Morayfield and support the safe, accurate and compliant management of investigational products used in clinical research. Health, Safety and Wellbeing Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super, People and Culture, Professional Make a meaningful impact at UniSC by strengthening workplace safety, supporting our people to thrive and helping shape a culture of wellbeing, respect and inclusion. Lecturer in First Nations Contemporary Art and Design (Identified position) UniSC Sunshine Coast Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Business and Creative Industries Shape the future of First Nations contemporary art and design at UniSC, embedding Indigenous knowledges, perspectives and creative practice into design education, research and engagement. Casual Academics (Nursing) Sunshine Coast Health Institute. UniSC Caboolture. UniSC Fraser Coast. UniSC Gympie. UniSC Sunshine Coast. UniSC Thompson Institute. UniSC Moreton Bay Academic, Casual Academic, Nursing, School of Health Join UniSC’s School of Health in 2027 as a Casual Academic (Nursing) and share your contemporary nursing expertise and professional experience with the next generation of nursing professionals. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
