    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/lecturer-in-paramedicine-unisc-sunshine-coast-qld-australia-4c78529d-454b-4a79-b413-104e851570bf": {
      "title": "Lecturer in Paramedicine",
      "description": "Lecturer in Paramedicine - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Lecturer in Paramedicine UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 Academic LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super School of Health Full-Time Add to favourites View favourites School of Health | UniSC Sunshine Coast, Sippy Downs Level B, $118,481 - $140,567 p.a., plus up to 17% employer superannuation Full-time (36.25 hours per week), ongoing appointment The School of Health (SoH) Where Passion Meets Impact Are you eager to make a difference in health education and research? Join our dedicated team of researchers and educators at the School of Health (SOH). We have a strong focus on cultivating healthy minds, bodies, and environments through our teaching, research, and outreach efforts. With a purpose that extends regionally and impacts globally, we are committed to advancing knowledge in the health sector and improving the well-being of our communities. Together, let's create healthier communities now and for the generations to come. The Opportunity This is an exciting opportunity for a teaching-focused academic to join UniSC’s established Bachelor of Paramedicine program and play a key role in preparing the next generation of registered paramedics. As a Lecturer in Paramedicine, you will deliver engaging, contemporary teaching across the SC306 program, using your paramedicine expertise to create authentic learning experiences across classroom, simulation and practical settings. You will support students to build the knowledge, skills and confidence needed to become successful, job-ready graduates. You will also contribute to innovative work-integrated learning opportunities that connect students with diverse healthcare settings and the realities of contemporary paramedic practice, including regional and rural experiences. Working collaboratively with colleagues, industry and professional partners, you will help strengthen student outcomes while contributing to the School of Health’s teaching, scholarship, research and engagement activities. For more information, please visit us online: School of Health You will: Deliver high-quality, contemporary teaching across the Bachelor of Paramedicine, creating engaging learning experiences across classroom, simulation, practical and online environments; Develop and enhance curricula, assessment and learning activities that connect academic learning with contemporary paramedic practice and support students to become confident, job-ready graduates; Contribute to high-quality work-integrated learning opportunities, including regional and rural experiences, while building meaningful relationships with industry, professional and community partners; and Contribute to scholarship, research and academic activities within the School of Health, supporting student success and the continued development of the Paramedicine discipline. About you: You will be a passionate and student-focused Paramedicine educator with contemporary disciplinary expertise and a genuine commitment to preparing graduates for professional practice. You will bring strong communication and interpersonal skills, an engaging approach to teaching, and the ability to connect academic learning with authentic paramedic practice. You will be confident working with students across diverse learning environments and committed to creating inclusive, practical and engaging learning experiences. You will value collaboration and bring an ability to build productive relationships with colleagues, industry and professional partners. Your commitment to ongoing professional development and contemporary paramedicine practice will support your contribution to student success and the broader academic community. You will possess: Completion of a relevant degree, postgraduate qualifications as well as registration with the Paramedicine Board of Australia; Effectiveness as a teacher, which is evidenced by: student feedback on teaching using valid instrument/s, peer review and/or student outcomes, and the capacity to conceive, develop and deliver higher education curricula and contribute to relevant areas of teaching; Membership of and sound connections with relevant professional bodies and community groups and/or experience in professional practice; Strong personal qualities and collegial approaches that contribute to the development and maintenance of a positive academic environment which is conducive to high levels of engagement and standards of achievement for both staff and students; and Evidence of participation in academic development activities and the desire to continue to learn and improve as an effective academic. Desirable Willingness to enrol or enrolment in a Higher Degree by Research in a relevant field; Experience undertaking academic administrative functions, e.g. course coordination within a University; and Experience in clinical placement. Don't meet every requirement? At UniSC, we understand that your work and life experiences can be just as valuable. If you're excited about this role but your CV doesn't align perfectly with our position description, we encourage you to apply anyway. You may be just the right candidate for this or one of our many other opportunities. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. How to apply All applications must be lodged through our website. To apply please visit our website at: Careers at UniSC Applications for this position close midnight, Sunday 25 October 2026. Position description: 494910_Lecturer in Paramedicine.pdf Your completed application must include: a resume, and a response to selection criteria. Noting that within the application form, we will request a statement addressing each of the selection criteria contained within the position description. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team. We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Associate Professor Nigel Barr Discipline Lead, Paramedicine – School of Health Telephone: 07 5456 5020 Email: nbarr@usc.edu.au UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. Flexible work arrangements & generous leave options. Salary packing options + 17% Super. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Trials Associate - Pharmacy Health Hub Morayfield Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Join UniSC Clinical Trials at Health Hub Morayfield and support the safe, accurate and compliant management of investigational products used in clinical research. Health, Safety and Wellbeing Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super, People and Culture, Professional Make a meaningful impact at UniSC by strengthening workplace safety, supporting our people to thrive and helping shape a culture of wellbeing, respect and inclusion. Lecturer in First Nations Contemporary Art and Design (Identified position) UniSC Sunshine Coast Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Business and Creative Industries Shape the future of First Nations contemporary art and design at UniSC, embedding Indigenous knowledges, perspectives and creative practice into design education, research and engagement. Associate Professor in Urgent Care UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LD $174,423 - $192,092 +17% super, School of Health Lead the future of urgent care education and research while shaping practical learning, supporting academic capability and building strong connections with the health sector. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
