iSC Clinical Trials at Health Hub Morayfield and support the safe, accurate and compliant management of investigational products used in clinical research. Health, Safety and Wellbeing Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super, People and Culture, Professional Make a meaningful impact at UniSC by strengthening workplace safety, supporting our people to thrive and helping shape a culture of wellbeing, respect and inclusion. Lecturer in First Nations Contemporary Art and Design (Identified position) UniSC Sunshine Coast Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Business and Creative Industries Shape the future of First Nations contemporary art and design at UniSC, embedding Indigenous knowledges, perspectives and creative practice into design education, research and engagement. Associate Professor in Urgent Care UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LD $174,423 - $192,092 +17% super, School of Health Lead the future of urgent care education and research while shaping practical learning, supporting academic capability and building strong connections with the health sector. Join our talent community! Sign up for job alerts First Name (required) fb784b09 Last Name (required) 38cbd46a Email (required) 0af7b7e6 Job Alert 42c60d12 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Australian Centre for Pacific Islands Research Casual Professional Centre for Bioinnovation Centre for Human Factors and Systems Science Forest Research Institute Thompson Institute UniSC Indigenous and Transcultural Research Centre Australian Centre for Pacific Islands Research Casual Professional Centre for Bioinnovation Centre for Human Factors and Systems Science Forest Research Institute Thompson Institute UniSC Indigenous and Transcultural Research Centre Employment Type Casual Casual Locations UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia UniSC Thompson Institute, QLD, Australia UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia UniSC Thompson Institute, QLD, Australia Send Please wait... Done Not You? Congratulations from the UniSC Talent Acquisition Team, you are now signed up for UniSC job alerts. Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) e6cda70b Last Name (required) 1427cde2 Email (required) e5ae15ae Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:17 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:17 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept Please choose the location(s)"
