    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/expression-of-interest-unisc-gym-and-fitness-attendants-casual-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-australia-unisc-caboolture-qld-unisc-sunshine-coast": {
      "title": "Expression of Interest: UniSC Gym and Fitness Attendants (Casual)",
      "description": "Expression of Interest: UniSC Gym and Fitness Attendants (Casual) - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES Expression of Interest: UniSC Gym and Fitness Attendants (Casual) UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Casual Professional L4 $50.41per hour (casual) UniSC Sport Casual Add to favourites View favourites UniSC Sport and Fitness | UniSC Moreton Bay, Petrie or UniSC Caboolture Level 4 - $48.82 per hour plus 12% superannuation Casual opportunity The Opportunity Are you passionate about health, fitness, and sport? UniSC is seeking expressions of interest from qualified gym and fitness professionals to join our vibrant and diverse community at UniSC Moreton Bay and UniSC Caboolture. As UniSC continues to grow, our Sport and Fitness team plays a key role in managing world-class facilities and delivering exceptional user experiences across all aspects of health, fitness, and sporting activities. With nationally accredited venues and support from leading health and sports scientists, UniSC has become a premier sporting destination. Here, high-performance athletes train alongside beginners in a supportive community that celebrates growth, passion, and excellence. For more information, please visit us online: UniSC Sport You will contribute to the coordination of the daily operations of the Gym and Sports Court at the Moreton Bay and Caboolture campuses; support the design, implementation, and delivery of exercise prescription services for gym members and patrons; assist in facilitating numerous internal university programs operating out of UniSC Sport and Fitness; and provide a safe, clean, and maintained daily training environment for all users and staff, across all Sport and Fitness facilities. To be successful you will possess completion of an associate diploma level qualification with relevant work-related experience or an alternate combination of relevant knowledge, training and experience. A Sport and Exercise Science degree would be highly regarded; experience with exercise program design and delivery; excellent client service skills with the ability to motivate and encourage clients. completion of a First aid and CPR qualification; and possess or be eligible to apply for a blue card (working with children check). UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. All applications must be lodged through the Careers at UniSC website. UniSC values a diverse and talented workforce and invites applications from candidates who already have legal work rights in Australia. UniSC does not accept unsolicited applications. For agency inquiries, contact unisc-careers@usc.edu.au Applications for this expression of interest talent pool close: midnight, Tuesday 30 September 2025. Your completed application must include: a resume, noting your application will be reviewed in alignment to the specified selection criteria as outlined within the job advertisement. There will be opportunity within the application form to also include supporting documentation should you wish. Further information regarding how to prepare your application is available on our website: Join our team We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at: Welcome to UniSC and LinkedIn Life Have questions or want to know more? For a confidential discussion, please contact: Troy Mytton Gym and Aquatic Coordinator - UniSC Sport and Fitness Email: tmytton@usc.edu.au Discover UniSC We're all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. We’re not the biggest university. But we’re growing every day, and doing big things. Like ground-breaking research, championing sustainability, producing gold-winning athletes and award-winning alumni. We're one of the fastest growing universities in Australia, growing to over 2,000 people across 5 campuses in South East Queensland. Teaching excellence is at the heart of what we do, and our commitment to sustainability is integrated into our teaching, research, and daily operations. Our research tackles the most pressing challenges of our time, with 13 research fields ranked well above world standard, characterised by evidence of outstanding performance according to the Excellence Research for Australia Rankings. At UniSC you will have the opportunity to contribute to the educational landscape for future generations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment, encouraging continuous professional development and providing resources to enhance your career. We recognise and value the contributions of each team member to our culture and success. We're not afraid to be different, and we're looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team that is working together to improve our local and global challenges. Our Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. EAP, fitness passport & discounted private health. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:47 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:47 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES Apply now! Enter your details below to commence your application: First Name (required) 9a184c39 Last Name (required) 5bb45fa8 Email (required) c900e6c3 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 3:17 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 3:17 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtit