    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/eoi-research-assistant-school-based-talent-pool-unisc-fraser-coast-qld-australia-unisc-sunshine-coast-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-unisc-caboolture-unisc-gympie": {
      "title": "EOI: Research Assistant (school-based) talent pool",
      "description": "EOI: Research Assistant (school-based) talent pool - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia - UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia - UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES EOI: Research Assistant (school-based) talent pool UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia, 4655 UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia, 4570 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Show More Show Less Casual Professional School of Business and Creative Industries School of Education and Tertiary Access School of Health School of Law and Society School of Science, Technology and Engineering Show More Show Less Casual Add to favourites View favourites EOI: Casual Research Assistant Talent Pool (school-based) Discover Casual Opportunities Across UniSC. Whether your background is in education, health, science, engineering, business, law, the creative industries, or any other field, we welcome your interest in joining our dynamic academic community. At UniSC, our research aims to deliver new perspectives and fresh insights that propels knowledge, action, and impact. We build strong research partnerships with industry and community to deliver research that makes a difference. As a casual research assistant, you’ll be working with world-class research teams as part of a supportive environment that values flexibility, inclusivity, and meaningful contribution to research excellence. Research assistant roles may involve: Conducting literature reviews Preparing ethics and grant applications Project management and stakeholder engagement Participant recruitment and engagement Supporting data collection and analysis Maintaining research databases and records Assisting in preparing research outputs and reports Key Requirements Completion of an AQF+1 qualification (e.g. Honours, Masters, PhD) in a relevant field Highly effective written and oral communicator Capacity to work independently and as part of a team (Desirable) Active engagement with industry, professional bodies, or community groups Why Join UniSC? At UniSC, we’re growing fast and doing big things. We’re home to award-winning alumni, gold medal-winning athletes, and groundbreaking researchers. We value collaboration, inclusion, and impact—and we’re proud to be one of the fastest growing universities in Australia. We offer: A welcoming, collaborative academic culture Modern facilities and campuses across South East Queensland Ongoing professional development opportunities Recognition of equity and diversity through initiatives like the Athena SWAN Bronze Award Access to support services such as EAP and discounted health care UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. How to Apply To express your interest, please submit your express of interest together with: A current resume with a focus on your research-related skills and experience including your familiarity with any relevant software Copies of relevant qualifications Working towards a better tomorrow We're all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. We’re not the biggest university. But we’re growing every day, and doing big things. Like ground-breaking research, championing sustainability, producing gold-winning athletes and award-winning alumni. We're one of the fastest growing universities in Australia, growing to over 2,000 people across 5 campuses in South East Queensland. Teaching excellence is at the heart of what we do, and our commitment to sustainability is integrated into our teaching, research, and daily operations. According to the 2023-24 Good Universities Guide we are Australia's highest rated public university for postgraduate teaching quality, skills development and student support and Australia's number one public university for overall postgraduate student experience. Our research tackles the most pressing challenges of our time, with 26 research fields ranked at or above world standard according to the Excellence in Research for Australia Rankings. In 2023 we recorded the biggest improvement in Australia for research quality, moving up more than 331 places in the world rank. At UniSC you will have the opportunity to shape the educational landscape and inspire the minds of future generations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment, encouraging continuous professional development and providing resources to enhance your teaching and research endeavours. We recognise and value the contributions of each team member to our culture and success. We're not afraid to be different, and we're looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team that is working together to improve our local and global challenges. We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at https://www.linkedin.com/school/university-of-the-sunshine-coast/life Please note: To maintain currency of this register, applicants will be notified via email when the pool will be re-advertised, with a link to re-apply if you wish to be considered for future opportunities. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Trials Associate - Pharmacy Health Hub Morayfield Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Join UniSC Clinical Trials at Health Hub Morayfield and support the safe, accurate and compliant management of investigational products used in clinical research. Health, Safety and Wellbeing Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super, People and Culture, Professional Make a meaningful impact at UniSC by strengthening workplace safety, supporting our people to thrive and helping shape a culture of wellbeing, respect and inclusion. Lecturer in First Nations Contemporary Art and Design (Identified position) UniSC Sunshine Coast Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Business and Creative Industries Shape the future of First Nations contemporary art and design at UniSC, embedding Indigenous knowledges, perspectives and creative practice into design education, research and engagement. Associate Professor in Urgent Care UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LD $174,423 - $192,092 +17% super, School of Health Lead the future of urgent care education and research while shaping practical learning, supporting academic capability and building strong connections with the health sector. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do