    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/eoi-office-of-research-research-assistant-talent-pool-unisc-fraser-coast-qld-australia-unisc-sunshine-coast-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-unisc-caboolture-unisc-gympie": {
      "title": "EOI: Office of Research / Research Assistant talent pool",
      "description": "EOI: Office of Research / Research Assistant talent pool - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia - UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia - UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES EOI: Office of Research / Research Assistant talent pool UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia, 4655 UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia, 4570 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Show More Show Less Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Casual Professional Casual Add to favourites View favourites Casual staff – Office of Research/Research Assistants Discover opportunities for casual employment within our research management team at UniSC. Interested in exploring suitable roles aligned with your expertise? Express your interest to join our community when suitable opportunities arise. UniSC’s Office of Research is dedicated to supporting and facilitating a diverse array of research activities. From securing funding and developing partnerships to promoting high quality research through ethics and research integrity, our team fosters a vibrant research culture that empowers researchers to explore new ideas, tackle complex challenges, and make a meaningful impact on society. Primary Objectives: Assist in the preparation and submission of research grant applications and funding proposals. Support the development and maintenance of partnerships with external stakeholders and research collaborators. Ensure compliance with research ethics and integrity guidelines, assisting with the preparation of ethics applications and monitoring processes. Review research contracts and agreements. Desirable Qualifications or Skills: Experience in research management. Strong organisational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and projects. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, with the ability to convey information clearly and effectively. Experience in providing comprehensive administrative support for the finalisation and execution of contracts, including liaising with stakeholders, ensuring compliance with due diligence policies, and identifying potential risks. Ability to work collaboratively within a team and with external partners. Relevant qualifications or experience. By joining us, you'll have the opportunity to contribute to cutting-edge research projects and collaborate with leading researchers. If you're passionate about research, innovation, and discovery, we encourage you to register your expression of interest. Working towards a better tomorrow We're all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. We’re not the biggest university. But we’re growing every day, and doing big things. Like ground-breaking research, championing sustainability, producing gold-winning athletes and award-winning alumni. We're one of the fastest growing universities in Australia, growing to over 2,000 people across 5 campuses in South East Queensland. Teaching excellence is at the heart of what we do, and our commitment to sustainability is integrated into our teaching, research, and daily operations. According to the 2023-24 Good Universities Guide we are Australia's highest rated public university for postgraduate teaching quality, skills development and student support and Australia's number one public university for overall postgraduate student experience. Our research tackles the most pressing challenges of our time, with 26 research fields ranked at or above world standard according to the Excellence in Research for Australia Rankings. In 2023 we recorded the biggest improvement in Australia for research quality, moving up more than 331 places in the world rank. At UniSC you will have the opportunity to shape the educational landscape and inspire the minds of future generations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment, encouraging continuous professional development and providing resources to enhance your teaching and research endeavours. We recognise and value the contributions of each team member to our culture and success. We're not afraid to be different, and we're looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team that is working together to improve our local and global challenges. Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. EAP & discounted private health. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. Contact People and Culture for further information : UniSC-careers@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at https://www.linkedin.com/school/university-of-the-sunshine-coast/life Please note: To maintain currency of this register, applicants will be notified via email when the pool will be re-advertised, with a link to re-apply if you wish to be considered for future opportunities. < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNTIES About UniSC For more information about UniSC's employment benefits and culture, including employee blogs, visit our employer information page . Recommended for you Clinical Trials Associate - Pharmacy Health Hub Morayfield Clinical Trials, Individual contributor, L5 $82,843 - $93,358 +17% super Join UniSC Clinical Trials at Health Hub Morayfield and support the safe, accurate and compliant management of investigational products used in clinical research. Health, Safety and Wellbeing Business Partner UniSC Sunshine Coast L8 $118,986 - $134,756 +17% super, People and Culture, Professional Make a meaningful impact at UniSC by strengthening workplace safety, supporting our people to thrive and helping shape a culture of wellbeing, respect and inclusion. Lecturer in First Nations Contemporary Art and Design (Identified position) UniSC Sunshine Coast Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander, Academic, LB $118,481 - $140,567 +17% super, School of Business and Creative Industries Shape the future of First Nations contemporary art and design at UniSC, embedding Indigenous knowledges, perspectives and creative practice into design education, research and engagement. Associate Professor in Urgent Care UniSC Sunshine Coast Academic, LD $174,423 - $192,092 +17% super, School of Health Lead the future of urgent care education and research while shaping practical learning, supporting academic capability and building strong connections with the health sector. LEGAL Privacy Copyright Disclaimer Right to Information Data Collection Preferences The University of the Sunshine Coast acknowledges the Traditional Custodians of the land on which we live, work and study. We pay our respects to local Indigenous Elders past, present and emerging and recognise the strength, resilience and capacity of all Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander people. ABN 28 441 859 157 | CRICOS Provider No. 01595D | TEQSA Provider No. PRV12082 Candidate Details This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. By continuing, you agree that you have read our Privacy Statement I do not accept I accept"
    },
    "https://careers.usc.edu.au/jobs/eoi-library-services-talent-pool-unisc-fraser-coast-qld-australia-unisc-sunshine-coast-unisc-moreton-bay-queensland-unisc-caboolture-unisc-gympie": {
      "title": "EOI: Library Services talent pool",
      "description": "EOI: Library Services talent pool - UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia - UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia - UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia - UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia - UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia Contact Us Candidate login Explore Opportunities Academic jobs Professional jobs Casual jobs Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander jobs Recruitment process Employer information Applicant Settings Kiosk mode < BACK TO EXPLORE OPPORTUNITIES EOI: Library Services talent pool UniSC Caboolture, QLD, Australia, 4510 UniSC Fraser Coast, QLD, Australia, 4655 UniSC Gympie, QLD, Australia, 4570 UniSC Sunshine Coast, QLD, Australia, 4556 UniSC Moreton Bay, Queensland, Australia, 4502 Show More Show Less Aboriginal and Torres Strait Islander Casual Professional Casual Add to favourites View favourites Casual staff – Library Services Discover opportunities for casual employment in our Library Services team! The library is a central hub for collaboration, research and lifelong learning at UniSC. Our people enjoy working in partnership to support the university community with access to inclusive space, quality services and current collections. Casual Student Library Assistant: Position description: Deliver frontline library services to assist students, staff and community in locating and accessing library resources, including books, journals, and online guides. Maintain the library's collections, ensuring resources are current, organised, and easily accessible. Offer technology support for library users, including assistance with digital resources, library software, and equipment. Participate in outreach activities to promote library services and resources to the university community. Desirable skills and qualifications: Current UniSC student (undergraduate or postgraduate), with at least 12 months remaining in their studies. Strong organisational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a customer focused approach to service delivery. Proficiency in using technology (Microsoft applications desirable). Casual Client Services Assistant: Position description: Assist students, staff, and clients in locating and accessing library resources, including books, journals, and online databases, in-person and online. Provide reference and information support and guidance, helping users develop effective search strategies and utilise library tools. Maintain the library's collections, ensuring resources are current, organised, and easily accessible. Offer technology support for library users, including assistance with digital resources, library software, and equipment. Conduct library orientation sessions and workshops to educate users on available services and resources. Participate in outreach activities to promote library services and resources to the university community. Desirable skills and qualifications: Experience/qualification in library services or information management. Strong organisational and time management skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and priorities. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills, with a customer focused approach to service delivery. Proficiency in using library management systems, online databases, and digital resources. Strong problem-solving abilities and attention to detail. By joining our team, you'll have the opportunity to promote access to information and enhance the overall academic experience for students and staff at UniSC. If you're passionate about libraries, technology, and empowering others through information, we encourage you to register your expression of interest. Working towards a better tomorrow We're all about doing work that matters, connecting with great people, and being part of an incredible journey. We’re not the biggest university. But we’re growing every day, and doing big things. Like ground-breaking research, championing sustainability, producing gold-winning athletes and award-winning alumni. We're one of the fastest growing universities in Australia, growing to over 2,000 people across 5 campuses in South East Queensland. Teaching excellence is at the heart of what we do, and our commitment to sustainability is integrated into our teaching, research, and daily operations. According to the 2023-24 Good Universities Guide we are Australia's highest rated public university for postgraduate teaching quality, skills development and student support and Australia's number one public university for overall postgraduate student experience. Our research tackles the most pressing challenges of our time, with 26 research fields ranked at or above world standard according to the Excellence in Research for Australia Rankings. In 2023 we recorded the biggest improvement in Australia for research quality, moving up more than 331 places in the world rank. At UniSC you will have the opportunity to shape the educational landscape and inspire the minds of future generations. We foster a collaborative and supportive environment, encouraging continuous professional development and providing resources to enhance your teaching and research endeavours. We recognise and value the contributions of each team member to our culture and success. We're not afraid to be different, and we're looking for people who share our values and want to be part of a team that is working together to improve our local and global challenges. Culture & Benefits: Our collaborative, passionate and welcoming culture is what really sets us apart. Modern teaching & research facilities. Professional development and career pathway opportunities. We are a proud recipient of the prestigious Athena SWAN Bronze Award, granted as part of the Science in Australia Gender Equity (SAGE) initiative. EAP& discounted private health. UniSC is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion. We encourage applications from all backgrounds, including those with disabilities, women in STEM, First Nations Peoples, and individuals of diverse cultures, genders, abilities, and experiences. We value achievement relative to opportunity and encourage your commentary on your achievements in this context. For additional support during the application process, please contact us at unisc-careers@usc.edu.au or call +61 7 5430 2830. Contact People and Culture for further information : UniSC-careers@usc.edu.au We would love the opportunity to get to know you better, but we know it works both ways. To get to know a little more about us, visit us at https://www.linkedin.com/school/university-of-the-sunshine-coast/life Please note: To maintain currency of this register, applicants will be notified via email when the pool will be re-advertised, with a link to re-apply if you wish to be considered for future opportunities. Video Player is loading. Play Video Play Skip Backward Skip Forward Mute Current Time 0:00 / Duration 1:47 Loaded : 0.00% 0:00 Stream Type LIVE Seek to live, currently behind live LIVE Remaining Time - 1:47 1x Playback Rate Chapters Chapters Descriptions descriptions off , selected Subtitles subtitles settings , opens subtitles settings dialog subtitles off , selected Audio Track Picture-in-Picture Fullscreen This is a modal window. Beginning of dialog window. Escape will cancel and close the window. Text Color White Black Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Text Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Opaque Semi-Transparent Transparent Caption Area Background Color Black White Red Green Blue Yellow Magenta Cyan Opacity Transparent Semi-Transparent Opaque Font Size 50% 75% 100% 125% 150% 175% 200% 300% 400% Text Edge Style None Raised Depressed Uniform Drop shadow Font Family Proportional Sans-Serif Monospace Sans-Serif Proportional Serif Monospace Serif Casual Script Small Caps Reset Done Close Modal Dialog End of dialog window. < BACK TO E